WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.977
Sandboxed AI models

00:00:01.789 --> 00:00:02.967
can still secretly

00:00:02.779 --> 00:00:03.404
talk

00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:05.085
Researchers showed

00:00:04.897 --> 00:00:05.828
two models on

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.748
the same vLLM

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.739
inference server can

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:08.564
communicate through

00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:09.484
side channels in

00:00:09.296 --> 00:00:10.156
how kernels are

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:10.616
chosen

00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:11.713
with no shared

00:00:11.525 --> 00:00:13.057
files or messages

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:14.372
In a color

00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:15.079
guessing game

00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:16.376
the receiving model

00:00:16.188 --> 00:00:17.131
got the sender's

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:18.004
color right in

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:20.669
all 1,221 rounds

00:00:21.206 --> 00:00:22.161
In a monitoring

00:00:21.973 --> 00:00:22.573
test

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:23.953
a colluding monitor

00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:24.779
let through all

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.606
354 attacks

00:00:26.831 --> 00:00:28.092
while still catching

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.062
85 to 92 percent

00:00:29.873 --> 00:00:30.875
of honeypots

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.412
Full story on

00:00:32.223 --> 00:00:33.119
the dashboard
